WEBVTT

00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:23.420
<i>I joined the concert band back in the
spring of my first year in high school.</i>

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:25.790
<i>This is the story of the six seasons
that have passed since then.</i>

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:27.790
<i>A story of miraculous chance encounters,</i>

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:30.000
<i>unravelled mysteries,</i>

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.420
<i>and the secrets that dwell
in people's hearts.</i>

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:38.300
Loosen up, Chika-chan.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:40.100
You've taken up a really weird pose.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:43.770
Homura-senpai, if you look that tense,

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:46.480
you'll make the rest of us anxious too.

00:00:46.970 --> 00:00:50.820
But who would've thought
we'd make it this far?

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:53.860
Tell me about it.
It's a miracle we're standing here at all.

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:55.830
Yeah...

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:57.360
It's all one big miracle.

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:00.790
<i>Getting to play the flute on stage,</i>

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:03.740
<i>reuniting with Haruta,</i>

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:07.820
<i>and meeting Kusakabe-sensei.</i>

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:13.230
<i>I don't know how or why,</i>

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:18.760
<i>but adolescence is always
full of unsolvable mysteries.</i>

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:20.650
Good morning, Homura-san.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:23.990
Today's the day you finally join us, right?

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:25.700
The volleyball team's waiting for you!

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:27.490
Well, you can stop waiting.

00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:30.700
My mind's already made up.

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:32.800
Wait, Homura-san!

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:35.590
You were such an amazing libero
back in junior high!

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:38.250
Not to mention your leg strength
and jumping ability!

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:43.380
And receiving skills.

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:47.120
Seriously, you were meant
to join the volleyball team!

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:48.320
What's holding you back?

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:49.770
Is it an injury?

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:51.340
Teammate issues?

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:53.250
A sudden desire to try a new sport?

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:55.030
None of the above.

00:02:55.580 --> 00:03:00.150
Junior high volleyball was like a year-round job,
and pulling overtime was the norm.

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:03.480
Be it Sundays, public holidays,
Christmas, or Valentine's,

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:04.740
there were no days off.

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:07.630
Sick of the constant practice,

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:11.160
I started to wonder if I really wanted
to spend my youth this way.

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:12.660
That's when...

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:14.640
I happened to see it.

00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:20.390
The All-Japan High School
Concert Band Competition!

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:27.170
In that moment, I knew what kind of
high school girl I wanted to become.

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:33.070
So I got my grandma to buy me this
as an enrolment gift.

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:38.900
From here on, I'll walk the path
of an elegant, cute girl.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.620
I don't like your chances, but good luck!

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:46.530
Do your best!

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:47.370
Hang in there!

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:50.120
The volleyball team will
always be waiting for you!

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:51.590
Waiting to welcome you with open arms!

00:03:51.590 --> 00:03:53.890
I'll reinvent myself for sure,

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:56.030
just you watchoo!

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:02.630
Are you all right?

00:04:04.130 --> 00:04:05.030
Yes.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:08.340
Seems like there's a lot of pollen
in the air this spring.

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:10.160
Use these, if you'd like.

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:12.930
Th-Thank you.

00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:15.020
How pretty.

00:04:16.070 --> 00:04:18.870
Your flute case is still brand new.

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:22.720
Are you going to join the concert band?

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:25.190
Yes, that's the plan.

00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:28.570
You can probably still find them
in the music room right now.

00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:31.520
It's just about time for
morning practice to end.

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:32.000
Uh...

00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:35.910
Oh, I'm Kusakabe, the music teacher.

00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:37.960
I only started last year, though.

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:44.210
I'm Homura Chika, of Class 1-2.

00:04:45.190 --> 00:04:48.140
I'm sure the band will
welcome you with open arms.

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:51.310
But I'm a complete beginner.

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:52.850
Don't worry.

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:54.980
You'll learn to play soon enough...

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:56.150
if you put in the effort.

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:57.490
Of course!

00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:00.230
The flute's a wonderful instrument,
don't you think?

00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:05.480
Its delicate and elegant tone
is almost like the singing of a bird.

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:06.990
Indeed.

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:08.590
<i>All right!</i>

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:11.240
<i>I'm playing the cute girl to perfection!</i>

00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:14.200
That must be the horn.

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:15.950
Such a nice sound.

00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:17.350
Who could that be?

00:05:19.430 --> 00:05:21.470
Smooth, silky hair,

00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:23.120
long eyelashes,

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:24.250
and double-edged eyelids...

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:26.350
Such an elegant and ladylike...

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:28.460
boy?!

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:33.350
Oh, good morning, Kusakabe-sensei!

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:35.160
Good morning, Kamijou-kun.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:37.050
Huh?

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:38.430
Chika-chan?

00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:40.000
"Chika-chan"?

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:42.050
Wait, "Kamijou-kun"?

00:05:42.050 --> 00:05:43.690
Is that you, Haruta?!

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:47.280
I mean, Kamijou-kun...

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:50.400
So the two of you were childhood friends?

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:51.470
That's right.

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:54.020
Our chance reunion really surprised me.

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:57.830
We were next-door neighbours
until grade school.

00:05:57.830 --> 00:05:58.830
It's been nine years, right?

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:00.550
Indeed.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:03.480
What's wrong, Chika-chan?

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:05.130
You were nothing if not energetic.

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:06.130
"Nothing"?

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:08.260
You don't mean that.

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:11.420
Remember how you used to
make me cry all the time?

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:12.760
Surely not.

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:13.980
You sure did.

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:15.930
You would place me in wrestling holds,

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:17.900
eat all my snacks,

00:06:18.280 --> 00:06:20.400
and stuff spotted frogs down my shirt.

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:23.980
Kamijou-kun, might you be
mistaking me for someone else?

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:24.900
Nope.

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:26.860
You also forced me to climb up trees

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:28.580
and play in puddles.

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:31.500
When we slid down that river bank,
I thought I was done—

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:32.910
Shaddup already!

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:36.780
I knew it. You haven't changed one bit.

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:42.300
Hey, Kamijou. Give me a hand here.

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:44.710
Oh, Prez. Sure, but first...

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:47.720
Sensei, there's something you need to see.

00:06:53.530 --> 00:06:54.680
What is this?

00:06:55.110 --> 00:06:57.120
When we came to the music room...

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:58.940
...for morning practice...

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:00.730
...we found these gross,
blood-like markings.

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:03.640
It's red paint.

00:07:04.010 --> 00:07:06.200
Who would do this?

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:09.060
It's like one of those
dying messages in horror movies.

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:10.480
You're the culprit?!

00:07:11.480 --> 00:07:13.350
This is Homura Chika-san.

00:07:13.350 --> 00:07:14.780
She'd like to join.

00:07:15.290 --> 00:07:16.450
Join?

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:18.150
Could you be any more misleading?

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:20.340
Sorry about that.

00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:21.810
Is that a flute?

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:22.900
Yes.

00:07:22.900 --> 00:07:25.210
At last, we have five members.

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:26.500
Five?

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:29.640
Wait, just five in total?

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:31.310
Four, without you.

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:33.920
So this is all of us?

00:07:34.290 --> 00:07:36.930
Yep. I'm Katagiri, the president.

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:38.850
I'm a second-year, and I play the trumpet.

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:42.120
These two are Asahina KaeSae,
also second-years.

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:43.160
Wrong way round.

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:45.000
And don't introduce us
like we're ManaKana.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:47.000
I'm Kae, the elder twin. I play the clarinet.

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:49.200
Sae, the younger twin. Bass tuba.

00:07:49.560 --> 00:07:51.880
Pleased to meet you.

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:54.920
Sorry to drop this on you right away,
but could you help me clean this off?

00:07:54.920 --> 00:07:55.990
Oh, sure...

00:07:55.990 --> 00:07:56.000
Hold on.
Oh, sure...

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:57.240
Hold on.

00:07:58.380 --> 00:08:01.410
This is no mere doodle.

00:08:02.390 --> 00:08:03.700
Look at this.

00:08:05.270 --> 00:08:06.670
"To Kusakabe-sensei".

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:12.340
"I'm sure you understand
....what this melody means".

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:14.880
This melody?

00:08:25.050 --> 00:08:28.320
Do you know this melody, Sensei?

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:29.480
No.

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:31.940
This is kinda creepy.

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:34.150
Aren't these white clovers?

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:35.990
What about them?

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:38.280
In floriography, white clovers stand for...

00:08:40.090 --> 00:08:41.400
...revenge.

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:50.010
Revenge?

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:52.960
Homeroom's about to begin.

00:08:53.450 --> 00:08:55.490
You should head to class.

00:08:55.490 --> 00:08:57.430
I'll clean up here.

00:08:57.430 --> 00:08:58.790
Okay.

00:08:58.790 --> 00:09:00.260
Kusakabe-sensei,

00:09:00.260 --> 00:09:03.380
please don't wipe out the score.

00:09:03.380 --> 00:09:05.910
It's probably a code.

00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:06.480
A code?

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:11.310
A message that only the sender
and intended recipient can decipher.

00:09:11.790 --> 00:09:13.530
I know that much.

00:09:14.010 --> 00:09:16.240
But it's clearly sheet music.

00:09:17.370 --> 00:09:20.730
It's a musical cryptogram.

00:09:20.730 --> 00:09:24.080
Sensei, you know about
the Art of the Fugue, right?

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:25.790
Bach, yes?

00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:28.150
What's that?

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:30.550
Surely even you've heard about it.

00:09:30.550 --> 00:09:31.880
Is it a detective novel?

00:09:32.330 --> 00:09:34.460
What, Bach is a mystery author now?

00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:36.570
Hey, I know who Bach is!

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:39.200
A man with hair like this, right?

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:40.390
Great, she's an idiot.

00:09:40.890 --> 00:09:45.330
The first detective story is said
to have been written in 1841.

00:09:45.330 --> 00:09:48.520
Edgar Allan Poe's
"The Murders in the Rue Morgue".

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:50.900
It was published close to
one hundred years after Bach died.

00:09:52.560 --> 00:09:56.930
The Art of the Fugue is an incomplete work
that Bach began writing in his final years.

00:09:56.930 --> 00:10:03.540
The phrase "Si flat-La-Do-Si"
repeatedly shows up in this piece.

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:06.110
This is the code.

00:10:06.110 --> 00:10:10.140
Si flat-La-Do-Si?

00:10:10.140 --> 00:10:12.020
And what would that be
in German notation?

00:10:12.020 --> 00:10:13.250
German notation?

00:10:13.980 --> 00:10:15.090
Chika-chan...

00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:17.890
You wanted to take up flute
without even knowing that?

00:10:17.890 --> 00:10:19.360
I'm a complete beginner.

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:21.260
Goes without saying that
I know absolutely nothing.

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:24.630
Do is C, pronounced "Ce" in German.

00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:28.180
C, D, E, F, G, A, H.

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:30.300
Si flat is B.

00:10:31.030 --> 00:10:31.850
Got it.

00:10:31.850 --> 00:10:34.320
Then what would this phrase be?

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:39.470
Si flat is B, then A, C...

00:10:39.470 --> 00:10:40.690
BACA?!

00:10:40.690 --> 00:10:42.380
The last one is H. Come on.

00:10:42.380 --> 00:10:43.200
Ah.

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:45.540
BACH, not BACA.

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:49.570
You just solved this musical cryptogram.

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:52.480
This is the Art of the Fugue.

00:10:52.480 --> 00:10:56.250
Bach put his own name in the score.

00:10:56.830 --> 00:11:00.760
So this score can be decoded the same way?

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:01.630
Nah.

00:11:01.630 --> 00:11:05.650
This doesn't look like a simple
conversion to German notation.

00:11:05.650 --> 00:11:07.600
All you get is gibberish.

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:12.050
What are these little digits?

00:11:12.050 --> 00:11:14.100
Homeroom's about to begin.

00:11:14.470 --> 00:11:18.270
I'll leave it up, but only until I go home.

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:19.800
Okay!

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:25.370
What makes you think it isn't just a doodle?

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:28.080
Don't you sense anything from it?

00:11:28.600 --> 00:11:29.720
What do you mean?

00:11:29.720 --> 00:11:32.070
You're so dense.

00:11:32.070 --> 00:11:34.860
What about you?
Can you solve that code?

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:38.230
I don't think they could've
made it all that difficult.

00:11:39.460 --> 00:11:44.050
The culprit is probably someone who went
to this school and graduated this year.

00:11:44.460 --> 00:11:45.760
How can you tell?

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:50.250
They know Kusakabe-sensei,
who only started working here last year,

00:11:50.250 --> 00:11:52.310
so they must've been
in this school last year.

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:57.200
And the reason they snuck into
the usually empty music room at night

00:11:57.200 --> 00:11:59.230
was because they couldn't
come here during the day.

00:11:59.230 --> 00:12:01.880
Which narrows it down
to this year's graduates.

00:12:01.880 --> 00:12:02.610
I see.

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:05.780
Judging from the message card,
they're left-handed,

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:09.570
and they must've romanised the message
in order to conceal their handwriting.

00:12:09.570 --> 00:12:14.040
Oh, the crown of white clovers
might stand for the number zero.

00:12:14.590 --> 00:12:17.210
Like, they resent Sensei for
giving them a zero on a test.

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:20.220
Must be nice to have
such a crazy imagination.

00:12:20.220 --> 00:12:21.380
What's that supposed to mean?

00:12:21.980 --> 00:12:25.680
You really haven't changed at all since then.

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:28.760
Say what? You haven't changed either!

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:31.260
You never show any tact
or know when to stop talking!

00:12:31.260 --> 00:12:33.250
And yet you pretend to be
this smart, mature guy!

00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:34.610
This is 1-1, you know?

00:12:37.660 --> 00:12:39.610
Pay more attention to your surroundings.

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:43.650
If you space out too much,
you'll let something important slip by unnoticed.

00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:45.310
I'm not spacing ou—

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:54.080
He seriously hasn't changed one bit!

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:57.260
Actually, he was way
more adorable as a kid!

00:12:57.620 --> 00:13:01.250
Well, maybe "adorable" is pushing it.

00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:03.150
Though I was just a child back then,

00:13:03.150 --> 00:13:05.370
so I might've been a bit rambunctious myself.

00:13:05.370 --> 00:13:07.180
You're funny, Homura-san.

00:13:07.550 --> 00:13:11.010
At first glance, you seemed
all mysterious and ladylike.

00:13:11.010 --> 00:13:12.560
But I ruined it by opening my mouth?!

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:16.460
Oh, no, you're just a little different
from your first impression.

00:13:16.460 --> 00:13:17.460
In a good way.

00:13:18.180 --> 00:13:19.450
Damn that Haruta.

00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:23.210
Now no one will see me as the elegant,
cute girl I planned to be.

00:13:23.210 --> 00:13:24.340
"Cute girl"?

00:13:24.340 --> 00:13:25.820
No, just you watch, Nozomi!

00:13:26.690 --> 00:13:27.320
Uh, sure!

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:32.950
I'll become a great flutist
and have people recognise me as a lady!

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:44.870
You really are a beginner, huh?

00:13:44.870 --> 00:13:46.110
Good posture, though.

00:13:46.110 --> 00:13:47.950
Probably has good lung capacity, too.

00:13:47.950 --> 00:13:50.290
If she didn't suck at playing,
she'd be perfect.

00:13:50.290 --> 00:13:50.680
Right?

00:13:51.310 --> 00:13:53.180
You don't need to dig that deep for praise.

00:13:53.180 --> 00:13:56.950
No, you're playing confidently,
without fear of failure.

00:13:56.950 --> 00:13:59.910
I'm sure you'll improve with practice.

00:13:59.910 --> 00:14:00.890
Thank you!

00:14:00.890 --> 00:14:03.660
But you'll have to practice alone for a while.

00:14:03.660 --> 00:14:05.440
Get started with the basic drills.

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:06.700
Okay.

00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:08.190
This way, Homura-san.

00:14:09.150 --> 00:14:14.240
I'm not much of an expert on the flute,
but I should be able to offer you some advice.

00:14:14.240 --> 00:14:15.790
Thank you very much!

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:18.780
You'll be good enough to practice
with the others before long.

00:14:19.440 --> 00:14:21.420
Welcome to the concert band.

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:24.600
Thank you for having me!

00:14:51.610 --> 00:14:53.280
Did you solve it?

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:57.250
I thought this code
was a substitution cipher...

00:14:57.250 --> 00:14:59.050
Sighfur?

00:14:59.050 --> 00:15:02.290
Code made using two sets of symbols,
horizontal and vertical.

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:04.580
For example, arrange
the musical scale horizontally,

00:15:04.580 --> 00:15:06.850
those little numbers vertically,

00:15:06.850 --> 00:15:08.770
and combine them to identify Japanese syllables.

00:15:08.770 --> 00:15:10.330
Do2 would be "i",

00:15:10.330 --> 00:15:12.040
and La3 would be "fu".

00:15:12.040 --> 00:15:15.930
I-fu-i-na-i-ni?

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:19.240
Yeah, it makes no sense.

00:15:19.240 --> 00:15:22.140
Those numbers only go up to three.

00:15:22.140 --> 00:15:25.220
Well, wipe the board clean
before you go home.

00:15:25.220 --> 00:15:26.250
Okay.

00:15:26.250 --> 00:15:27.860
We're out of time, huh?

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:30.190
I should take a picture.

00:15:31.600 --> 00:15:32.550
There.

00:15:32.550 --> 00:15:37.530
Oh, I should text my mum and tell her
that Haruta goes to my school.

00:15:37.910 --> 00:15:45.500
"Haruta's still a cheeky brat."

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:47.310
Let me see that, Chika-chan!

00:15:47.950 --> 00:15:49.320
I was only kidding.

00:15:50.830 --> 00:15:52.970
So it really was...

00:15:56.080 --> 00:15:57.090
"Affettuoso".

00:15:57.090 --> 00:15:58.970
A... what?

00:15:59.430 --> 00:16:01.340
It means "lovingly".

00:16:01.340 --> 00:16:03.180
With this, the score is complete.

00:16:03.640 --> 00:16:04.660
What do you mean?

00:16:04.660 --> 00:16:05.480
You solved it?

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:06.380
I did.

00:16:06.380 --> 00:16:07.520
What's it say?

00:16:08.080 --> 00:16:12.650
But this is a personal message
to Kusakabe-sensei.

00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:17.030
You solved it a long time ago, didn't you?

00:16:17.030 --> 00:16:18.530
All right, erase it.

00:16:18.530 --> 00:16:19.620
It's time to go home.

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:22.830
Huh? But we want to know
what's written, too.

00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:24.000
Same here!

00:16:28.980 --> 00:16:34.560
This is a simple code that combines
notes and numbers to identify a letter.

00:16:34.560 --> 00:16:37.470
But I didn't know what the actual table was.

00:16:38.360 --> 00:16:42.200
I thought they used romanised Japanese
to hide their handwriting,

00:16:42.200 --> 00:16:44.190
but it was actually a hint.

00:16:44.860 --> 00:16:46.160
Take a look.

00:16:46.160 --> 00:16:47.420
A keyboard?

00:16:47.420 --> 00:16:50.190
The keyboard has three rows of alphabetical letters.

00:16:50.190 --> 00:16:53.280
That's why these numbers only went up to three.

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:55.800
Do1 is I.

00:16:55.800 --> 00:16:56.740
L.

00:16:56.740 --> 00:16:57.910
O.

00:16:57.910 --> 00:17:00.150
I lo...

00:17:00.150 --> 00:17:01.490
"I love you."

00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:03.600
"Thank you."

00:17:04.600 --> 00:17:08.290
This is a love letter
addressed to Kusakabe-sensei.

00:17:08.730 --> 00:17:12.490
They wanted to tell him about their feelings,
but they were unable to.

00:17:13.150 --> 00:17:15.260
So they poured their feelings into this piece.

00:17:15.260 --> 00:17:17.610
But then what about the white clovers?

00:17:17.610 --> 00:17:20.460
White clovers don't just stand for revenge.

00:17:20.460 --> 00:17:23.470
They can also mean "Think about me".

00:17:24.350 --> 00:17:27.400
"I love you"...

00:17:28.100 --> 00:17:31.460
So the culprit is in love with Sensei?

00:17:31.460 --> 00:17:32.320
Culprit?!

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:36.530
Sensei, do you have any idea
who could've written this?

00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:38.080
A left-handed student
who graduated this year—

00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:39.220
Haruta!

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:40.990
Sensei...

00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:45.700
Yes, let's end our game of detective here.

00:17:45.700 --> 00:17:46.730
But...

00:17:46.730 --> 00:17:49.870
I want school to remain a place
where students are allowed diversions,

00:17:49.870 --> 00:17:53.420
as long as they find
what's precious to them.

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:55.460
I'll erase this.

00:17:55.460 --> 00:17:58.130
N-No, Sensei! We'll do it!

00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:45.810
Unrequited love can be so painful.

00:18:45.810 --> 00:18:51.440
I thought solving the riddle would help me
figure out Kusakabe-sensei's secret.

00:18:51.950 --> 00:18:53.890
Sensei's secret?

00:18:53.890 --> 00:18:57.680
He was a conductor with a promising future.

00:18:57.680 --> 00:18:59.290
Conductor...

00:18:59.290 --> 00:19:01.780
Kusakabe Shinjirou, twenty-six years old.

00:19:02.220 --> 00:19:06.500
As a student, he came runner-up in the
Tokyo international music competition,

00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:09.750
after which he was invited to study abroad.

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:12.960
But upon returning to Japan,

00:19:12.960 --> 00:19:15.290
he abandoned his career
and went into hiding for years.

00:19:15.710 --> 00:19:20.300
Until last year, when he came
to this school as a music teacher.

00:19:21.140 --> 00:19:23.960
Why do you know so much?

00:19:24.650 --> 00:19:26.310
Oh, I just heard rumours.

00:19:29.780 --> 00:19:30.850
Hay fever?

00:19:30.850 --> 00:19:32.370
Got any tissues?

00:19:32.370 --> 00:19:33.770
Nope.

00:19:34.730 --> 00:19:36.210
Hey, you've got your own!

00:19:36.210 --> 00:19:38.040
These ones are important to me.

00:19:39.190 --> 00:19:40.970
Wanna drop by and see my mum?

00:19:40.970 --> 00:19:43.590
Nah. I'm not hungry today.

00:19:43.590 --> 00:19:46.360
I never said anything about dinner.

00:19:46.360 --> 00:19:47.530
Later.

00:19:48.770 --> 00:19:49.490
Haruta!

00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:53.410
I hope we'll have lots of fun again.

00:19:53.410 --> 00:19:58.500
Chika-chan, if you can't manage at least scales soon,
you won't be able to take part in practice.

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:00.050
I know!

00:20:00.050 --> 00:20:02.300
That so? Well, good luck.

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:08.800
I'm so gonna get better than Haruta!

00:20:08.800 --> 00:20:14.150
I'll practice all year, even on Sundays,
public holidays, Christmas, and Valentine's!

00:20:14.150 --> 00:20:16.400
"You've grown so much better, Homura-san."

00:20:16.400 --> 00:20:18.360
"It's all thanks to you, Kusakabe-sensei!"

00:20:18.360 --> 00:20:19.360
Hug!

00:20:20.300 --> 00:20:21.180
Chika?

00:20:21.720 --> 00:20:22.780
Welcome back.

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:31.750
Morning!

00:20:33.170 --> 00:20:34.720
I'm off!

00:20:37.080 --> 00:20:38.500
In at 6:45!

00:20:39.090 --> 00:20:41.720
Don't underestimate a former
volleyball player, Haruta!

00:20:43.510 --> 00:20:45.240
This melody...

00:20:50.220 --> 00:20:52.920
Huh? You're early, Chika-chan.

00:20:52.920 --> 00:20:54.010
Here for morning practice?

00:20:54.010 --> 00:20:55.140
What about you?

00:20:55.980 --> 00:20:57.600
Why were you playing that piece?

00:21:07.170 --> 00:21:09.600
I guess you were paying attention after all.

00:21:11.160 --> 00:21:14.200
You like Kusakabe-sensei too, right?

00:21:14.200 --> 00:21:15.320
Wha—

00:21:16.060 --> 00:21:17.370
Wait, "too"?!

00:21:17.790 --> 00:21:20.350
Is that why you joined the concert band?

00:21:20.350 --> 00:21:21.380
Of course not!

00:21:21.870 --> 00:21:22.880
Thank goodness.

00:21:23.640 --> 00:21:26.300
I seriously want to go to All-Japans.

00:21:27.160 --> 00:21:32.200
I'm sure even the most minor concert bands
still have the right to aim for it.

00:21:32.200 --> 00:21:33.260
Me too!

00:21:33.260 --> 00:21:35.730
Then until we stand on the
hallowed stage at Fumon Hall,

00:21:35.730 --> 00:21:37.900
there'll be no stealing of
marches on each other.

00:21:37.900 --> 00:21:39.030
Got that?

00:21:39.030 --> 00:21:40.570
"Each other"?

00:21:40.570 --> 00:21:42.020
So you really are...

00:21:42.960 --> 00:21:45.030
I take both music and love very seriously.

00:21:46.190 --> 00:21:48.110
I won't lose to you just because I'm a guy.

00:21:48.950 --> 00:21:51.630
My rival in love is my childhood friend...

00:21:52.710 --> 00:21:53.770
and a boy?

00:21:54.370 --> 00:21:56.170
No way!

00:21:56.170 --> 00:22:00.230
I refuse to accept this love triangle!

00:23:31.430 --> 00:23:33.660
Narushima Miyoko, Class 1-3.

00:23:33.660 --> 00:23:34.440
You know of her?

00:23:34.440 --> 00:23:36.970
She's an outstanding talent
I want in our band at all costs.

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:37.890
You can't do it.

00:23:37.890 --> 00:23:40.390
That cube is impossible to solve.
